<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ June yr current account deficit NZ$3.657 bln.</title>
<headline>NZ June yr current account deficit NZ$3.657 bln.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics New Zealand on Friday released the following balance of payments data for the June 1996 quarter and the year to June.</p>
<p>Rounded actual figures, in millions of NZ dollars (- is deficit). &quot;Revised from&quot; figures are in brackets.</p>
<p>		    June 1996 qtr	Mar 1996 qtr    June 1995 qtr</p>
<p>Merch trade	  +740		  +247		   +893</p>
<p>Invisibles	  -1576		  -294 (-255)	 -1729</p>
<p>Balance		-836		  -47  (-8)	    -837</p>
<p>	  June year current account data</p>
<p>		     Yr-Jun 1996     Yr-Mar 1996	Yr-June 1995</p>
<p>Merch trade	    728		881		   1724</p>
<p>Invisibles	   -4385	    -4538 (-4499)	-5495</p>
<p>Balance		-3657	    -3657 (-3618)	-3771</p>
<p>SNZ said the deficit was 4.1 percent of GDP at June 30 vs 4.2 percent at March 31.</p>
<p>Note - economists forecast a quarterly account deficit of $550 million and an annual deficit of $3.41 billion.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 473 4746</p>
</text>
